From the manuals check (EastSun 20261001):
- Blend "right-click an object, point to Set Current Selection ... displays all objects in the
  hierarchy" (Blend 2012: "a list of all objects, in Z order ... under the location that you
  clicked"): the probe remembers the last right-click point and answers stackAt (elementsFromPoint
  -> components, the top one first, the form last); the command lists them in a QuickPick and
  selects the one picked. Pages with many panels stacked in one place (Alert.Note) no longer need
  Alt+click layer by layer.
- Order (front / forward / backward / back) moved only the primary one of a multi-selection. Now
  each selected one among its own siblings, their order kept (front / backward: the earliest first;
  back / forward: the latest first; a one-step move never jumps over a selected one that could not
  move), ONE edit.
The right-click menu's top level is 27 items now (the cap the smoke test keeps, + this one).
Tests: probe -- a right-click on the button = spbSave > Panel2 > @form; smoke -- front with
spbSave + Label1 = each last among its siblings, ONE edit; backward with both of Panel2's, the first
at the bottom = nothing changes; the list's second item picked = selectId Panel2. run_all 3/3
layers (lib 168, smoke 200).

